    {
      "slug": "isenheim-altarpiece",
      "title": "Isenheim Altarpiece",
      "year": 1512,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e2/Isenheim_Altarpiece_-_In_situ_%28cropped%29.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 4429,
      "imageHeight": 3468,
      "story": "The Isenheim Altarpiece is an altarpiece sculpted and painted by, respectively, the Germans Nikolaus Hagenauer and Matthias Grünewald in 1512–1516. It is on display at the Unterlinden Museum at Colmar, Alsace, in France. It is Grünewald's largest work and is regarded as his masterpiece.",
      "facts": [
        "Guy Guyers, who had commissioned the Altarpiece, is depicted kneeling at the feet of Saint Augustine.",
        "From 2018 to June 2022, a team of restorers led by Anthony Pontabry undertook a major cleaning and restoration of the altarpiece.",
        "Hagenauer's sculptures were restored in the polychrome wood restoration workshop in Paris of the Center for Research and Restoration of Museums of France by a team of sculpture restorers led by Juliette Levy.",
        "A study had been conducted by the Research Centre of the Musées de France in 2014 when they determined the state of the altarpiece and established the protocol for its restoration."
      ],
      "wikipediaUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isenheim_Altarpiece",
